# =============================================================================
# What never enters the build context.
#
# The `development` target ends in `COPY . .`, so without this file everything
# beside the Dockerfile is uploaded to the daemon and committed to a layer. Three
# separate problems, in descending order of how much they matter:
#
#   1. **Secrets.** `credentials.json` and `token.pickle` are the Gmail OAuth client
#      and a live refresh token. They are gitignored, so nothing else in the
#      pipeline would ever have caught them - and a layer is not a file you can
#      delete afterwards. Anyone who pulls the image reads them.
#   2. **A foreign virtualenv.** `.venv` here is built for the developer's own OS.
#      Copying a Windows venv into a Linux image is hundreds of megabytes of
#      unusable binaries, and if anything ever resolved it ahead of `/app/.venv`
#      the container would import pywin32 and die.
#   3. **Cache churn.** `.pytest_cache` and friends change on every local test run,
#      which invalidates the `COPY` layer and every layer after it - a rebuild for
#      a change to nothing.
#
# Everything the build actually needs is listed in the Dockerfile's own COPY lines:
# pyproject.toml, uv.lock, app/, migrations/, scripts/, alembic.ini, README.md.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.sample
credentials.json
token.pickle
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# ---- Virtualenvs (the image builds its own at /app/.venv) --------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Python build and cache artefacts ---------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ---- Runtime output ---------------------------------------------------------
# Mounted as a volume at /app/logs; a host copy would just be shadowed.
logs/
*.log

# ---- Uploaded documents -----------------------------------------------------
# The legacy filesystem blob directory. Customer data, and megabytes of it.
var/

# ---- Not needed inside the image --------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
